  "question": {
    "text": "Which element among the following cannot form an amphoteric oxide?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sn</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sb</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mtext>P</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Phosphorus being a non-metal always forms acidic oxides like <math><msub><mrow><mtext>P</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>P</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> etc. whereas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Sn</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sb</mi></math> are amphoteric elements.<br /><math><mtext>A</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mtext>S</mtext><mtext>n</mtext><mtext>O</mtext></math> and <math><mtext>S</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>b</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> are amphoteric oxides i.e., they can react with both acids as well as bases."
  }
